{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:81552",
  "title": "Important: kernel security update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-10-14 06:30:05"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-10-16 00:12:08"
  },
  "severity": "Important",
  "description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: drm/xe/uapi: Reject coh_none PAT index for CPU cached memory in madvise (CVE-2026-46309)\n\n* kernel: macsec: fix replay protection at XPN lower-PN wrap (CVE-2026-63925)\n\n* kernel: bpf: Support for hardening against JIT spraying (CVE-2026-64508)\n\n* kernel: x86/bugs: Enable IBPB flush on BPF JIT allocation (CVE-2026-64507)\n\n* kernel: drm/amd/display: set new_stream to NULL after release (CVE-2026-68236)\n\n* kernel: drm/dp/mst: fix buffer overflows in sideband chunk accumulation (CVE-2026-68278)\n\n* kernel: drm/amdgpu: fix lifetime issue of amdgpu_vm_get_task_info_pasid() (CVE-2026-68245)\n\n* kernel: openvswitch: fix GSO userspace truncation underflow (CVE-2026-68123)\n\n* kernel: cifs: validate DFS referral string offsets (CVE-2026-72318)\n\n* kernel: drm/vmwgfx: use check_add_overflow for shader size+offset bound (CVE-2026-80887)\n\n* kernel: nvmet-auth: Synchronize timeout work during SQ teardown (CVE-2026-89970)\n\n* kernel: drm/amdkfd: Add TLB flush after MES queue eviction/suspension (CVE-2026-89811)\n\n* kernel: media: cx231xx: reject geometry changes while the VBI queue is busy (CVE-2026-89894)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
